# redundant-parentheses fires on '(X)' (line 10, lone term) and '((X+1))'
# (line 11, nested); must NOT fire on '(X + 1)' (line 12, binary) nor on the
# single-element const array constructor '= (''x'')' (line 6, initializer ctx).
redundant-parentheses 10
redundant-parentheses 11
!redundant-parentheses 6
!redundant-parentheses 12
